### 3. Lightweight Indexing Scripts

**Problem:** Full indexer caused OOM even with cloud embeddings

**Solution 1:** `scripts/lightweight_indexer.py` (Markdown)
- Processes one file at a time
- Explicit garbage collection after each file
- Simple character-based chunking (4000 chars/chunk)
- Direct ChromaDB Cloud API calls

**Performance:**
- Successfully indexed all 21 markdown files without memory issues
- Total: 495 document chunks
- Uses OpenAI `text-embedding-3-small` model

**Solution 2:** `scripts/index_pdfs_and_zips.py` (PDFs + ZIP extraction)
- Extracts PDFs from ZIP archives automatically
- Skips PDFs larger than 15 MB (configurable)
- Processes one PDF at a time with PyPDF2
- Handles scanned/image PDFs gracefully

**Performance:**
- Successfully indexed 64 out of 66 PDFs
- Extracted and indexed 9 PDFs from ZIP files
- Total: 2,021 PDF chunks added
- Combined total: 2,516 chunks (495 markdown + 2,021 PDF)

